  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "What is the average value of $h(x)=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x$ on the interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2}]?$",
  "worked_solution": "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }{(\\frac{1}{2})(-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2x))|}_{\\pi /4}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }(-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
